# Sinfonia No. 4 in D minor, BWV 790 (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: grave and lamenting. A sighing, syncopated subject over a
# rising walking bass; chromatic lines (alto bars 12-13, top 20-23)
# give it the weight of a lament. It ends on a bare D.
#
# Tempo: quarter = 52. Timings for 23 bars: Andras Schiff (clavichord,
# ECM) 1:46, about 52; Angela Hewitt 1:40, about 55; Glenn Gould 3:15,
# about 28 (a very slow outlier). 52 follows Schiff and Hewitt.
#
# Structure (my reading of the Mutopia score):
#   1-8    subject top 1, mid 2 (A minor), bottom 4; cadence in A minor
#          bar 3; bass entry 6; cadence in F major bar 8 (beat 3).
#   8-13   entries in F: mid 8.5, top 9.5; sequence 11-12 with a
#          chromatic descent in the middle voice; cadence in A minor
#          bar 13 (beat 3).
#   13-19  stretto-like run of entries: top 13.5, mid 14.5, bottom
#          15.5 (G minor), top 16.5, mid 17.5; toward D minor.
#   20-23  cadence in D minor at bar 20 with the bass entry; the top
#          climbs chromatically to its high D (21), then falls
#          chromatically to the final D (23).

tempo 52
rit 2 0.7                 # bars 22-23: the chromatic fall to the end
broaden 19 0.94           # bar 19: into the D minor cadence and the return

dyn 1 mp                  # bars 1-8: the lament, restrained
dyn 8.5 mf                # bars 8-13: F major entries, after the cadence in F
dyn 13.5 mp               # bars 13-19: back to the minor keys, after the A minor cadence
dyn 20 mf                 # bars 20-21: tonic return and the climb to the high D
dyn 22 mp                 # bars 22-23: the chromatic descent, falling away

lead 1 top                # subject in the top
lead 2 mid                # answer in the middle (A minor)
lead 4 bottom             # subject in the bass
lead 6 bottom             # bass entry
lead 8.5-9 mid            # middle entry in F
lead 9.5-10 top           # top entry in F
lead 13.5-14 top          # top entry in A minor
lead 14.5-15 mid          # middle entry
lead 15.5-16 bottom       # bass entry in G minor
lead 16.5-17 top          # top entry
lead 17.5-18 mid          # middle entry
lead 20 bottom            # bass entry on the return to D minor
